# FastAPI Specific Cursor Rules

## API Design Patterns

- Use Pydantic models for all request/response schemas
- Implement proper HTTP status codes for each response
- Use dependency injection for shared resources (database, auth)
- Structure endpoints with clear REST conventions
- Use proper HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH)

## Request/Response Models

- Create separate Pydantic models for requests and responses
- Use Field() for additional validation and documentation
- Implement proper validation for all input fields
- Use Optional[] for nullable fields
- Add example values for better API documentation

## Error Handling

- Use HTTPException for client errors (400, 401, 403, 404)
- Return consistent error response format
- Log errors with request context
- Implement global exception handlers
- Use proper status codes for different error types

## Authentication & Authorization

- Implement proper JWT token handling
- Use dependency injection for auth verification
- Implement role-based access control
- Secure sensitive endpoints with proper decorators
- Use environment variables for secret keys

## Database Integration

- Use async database operations with SQLAlchemy
- Implement proper connection pooling
- Use database transactions for data consistency
- Implement proper error handling for database operations
- Use database migrations for schema changes

## API Documentation

- Use proper docstrings for all endpoints
- Include example requests and responses
- Document all parameters and response fields
- Use tags for organizing endpoints
- Implement proper OpenAPI documentation

## Performance

- Use async/await for I/O operations
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use background tasks for long-running operations
- Optimize database queries
- Monitor API response times

## Testing

- Write unit tests for all endpoints
- Use TestClient for API testing
- Mock external dependencies
- Test both success and error scenarios
- Use proper test fixtures and setup 